# Canonical identity for this repository.
#
# ALWAYS ON work is committed under the owner's single account, no matter which
# local tool, session, or agent made the change. Without this file GitHub builds
# its contributor list from raw commit identities, so any secondary identity (a
# tool's agent address, or a differently spelled name) shows up as a separate
# contributor. This file collapses every identity onto one account.
#
# Syntax:  <canonical-name> <canonical-email>  <source-name> <source-email>
# The canonical identity always comes FIRST; the commit identity to be folded
# in comes last.

# Unattended/autonomous commits made by tooling, not by a person.
300x3 <300x3@posteo.net> <ALWAYS ON Agent> <agent@300x3.com>
300x3 <300x3@posteo.net> <ALWAYSON Agent> <agent@300x3.com>

# Own commits recorded under a display name instead of the account name.
300x3 <300x3@posteo.net> <SCOTT WIDMANN> <300x3@posteo.net>
300x3 <300x3@posteo.net> 300x3@posteo.net <300x3@posteo.net>
